@* The series page's mute (feature-spec §4.5), in the Sync corner because it is about what the
   sync tells you. Only offered once some device has notifications on, or when the series is
   muted already so it can be unmuted. Mute is about pushes only: the series still shows in
   "Since your last visit". No aria-pressed: the label itself says what the button does next
   (Mute / Unmute) and the fine line above says the state, so "pressed" would only contradict. *@

@if (Notifications.HasDevices || Series.NotificationsMuted)
{
    <div class="mute">
        <p class="fine">
            @(Series.NotificationsMuted
                ? "Muted: no notifications about this series."
                : "New volumes and dates for this series are sent to your devices.")
        </p>
        <button type="button"
                class="ghost mute__toggle"
                disabled="@SeriesState.IsSaving"
                @onclick="ToggleAsync">
            @(Series.NotificationsMuted ? "Unmute" : "Mute this series")
        </button>
    </div>
}
